% ============================================================
% references.bib
% Shared bibliography for "La Jolla Move-In: Pancreatic Oncology Clinical Trial
% Site Complete Documentation Package".  Repository v4.7.0, August 23, 2026.
%
% PROVENANCE.  Assembled from four repository sources and nothing else:
%   funding/move-in/inputs/READMES/README-LLM-Pancreatic-Oncology-...md
%       (the twenty deposited papers, with dates and digital object identifiers)
%   funding/move-in/inputs/ChemicalQDevice_Accomplishments.docx
%       (the seventeen numbered references, including the 2024 preprints)
%   funding/move-in/inputs/Physical-AI-...-Package.zip, all_documents.bib
%       (the predecessor package's own author entries and California bills)
%   funding/pdac-funding-applications/final-apply/references.bib
%       (the policy entries and the codified-law entries reused here)
%
% CONVENTION.  Every entry that has a digital object identifier carries both a
% doi field and a url field pointing at https://doi.org/<doi>, so movestyle.sty
% renders the identifier as text with a clickable target and no link overflows
% the measure.  The style is unsrturl, not unsrt: plain unsrt.bst reads neither
% the doi nor the url field, so a reference list built on identifiers would
% print none of them and offer nothing to click.
%
% No identifier is invented.  The paper's own identifier is left in the
% placeholder form 10.5281/zenodo.xxxxxxxx by Rule 12 and is not a bib entry.
% ============================================================

